Unit Tests
==========

Spine's unit test suite uses libcheck (https://libcheck.github.io/check/).
The tests cover pure utility functions and config-file parsing.  Functions
that require a live MySQL handle or a Net-SNMP session are not included here;
those belong in the integration layer under tests/snmpv3/.

Prerequisites
-------------

libcheck >= 0.9.10 must be present at configure time.  On common platforms:

  macOS:   brew install check
  Debian:  apt-get install check
  RHEL:    yum install check-devel

Building
--------

  ./bootstrap          # regenerate autoconf/automake files
  ./configure          # check must appear in pkg-config output
  make

Running
-------

  make check

The check target builds and runs test_util and test_config.  Each binary
reports per-test pass/fail in CK_NORMAL format, then exits non-zero if any
test failed.

If libcheck is not found at configure time, a warning is printed and the
tests/ subdirectory is skipped silently.  The main spine binary is unaffected.

Test binaries
-------------

test_util    -- covers all_digits, is_ipaddress, is_hexadecimal, trim/rtrim/ltrim,
                reverse, strpos, char_count, strncopy, is_numeric

test_config  -- covers config_defaults (default values in global set struct)
                and read_spine_config (file parsing, directive handling,
                missing-file error path)

Sanitizer builds
----------------

Sanitizer builds run on every push/PR via `.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml`.
